• Malicious file upload checks to be in place- 
o File Name 
o File Name Length 
o File Size (minimum and maximum) minimum size -> 10 kb  , maximum size-> 50 mb
o File Type Whitelist  
o File Type length. 
o Multiple extension check 
• Additionally following file related checks should be imposed- 
o POST only. 
o Unrestricted file download 
o File path should not be visible in request/response to the end user. 
o Validate Headers: Content-Type, Content-Disposition, X-Content-Type-Options, Content
Security-Policy 
o Disable browser caching. 
o File permissions on storage. 
o Client side as well as server-side file restrictions should be implemented. 
o If it is excel file, check for macros and CSV injection related attacks. 
o No decompression should be allowed to bypass file size restrictions. 
o Filename change in format which is not guessable on upload success. 
o Metadata should also be sanitized or removed.  
o Restrict file name characters that are not allowed. 
• Malicious content should be filtered and sanitised adequately to protect SBI ecosystem. 
• Please ensure that file related attacks like below but not just limited the same are taken are of- 
? LFI 
? RFI 
? Unrestricted file download. 
? Do not display the file upload path in URL. 
? Forced browsing 
? Parameter manipulation 
? IDOR 
o Kindly take care of- 
? Injection attacks. 
? XSS (Reflected, DOM and Stored). 
• Unrestricted file download and force browsing to be taken care of. 
• Session management flaws to be taken care of. 
• MFA implementation may be considered. 
• Enforce principle of least privileges and role-based access controls. 
• Sensitive information should not be hardcoded. 
